---
description: Use Serena symbolic tools and read Serena project memories first
alwaysApply: true
---

Serena is the MCP coding toolkit for this repo. The server is `serena` in `.cursor/mcp.json` (wrapper `.cursor/serena-mcp.sh`, context `ide`, agent interface `tools`). `.cursor/install.sh` installs `uv` and `serena-agent` during Cloud Agent Builds.

At the start of a task, read `.serena/memories/`, beginning with `critical_info` and `core`, then the memories `core` references.

Prefer Serena symbolic tools (`get_symbols_overview`, `find_symbol`, `find_referencing_symbols`, `replace_symbol_body`, insert before or after a symbol) for navigation and code edits. Use a line-based edit only when there is no symbol to address.

Do not pass `--context ide-assistant`. That name is retired in current Serena and is not the Cursor context.

Documentation: write only under `Docs/` (capital D) as `.en.md` / `.ru.md` pairs (`Docs/specs/`, `Docs/qa/`). Link to the matching language suffix.
